      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Since beta-tryptase is considered a critical mediator of asthma, potent tryptase inhibitors may be useful as new agents for the treatment of asthma. We investigated 4-substituted benzylamine derivatives and obtained M58539 (15h) as a potent inhibitor of beta-tryptase (IC50 = 5.0 nM) with high selectivity against other serine proteases, low molecular weight, clog P value less than 5, lack of amidino and guanidino groups, and independence of Zn2+ ion."},
